==== simple
h2: High Availability - General
Configure a high availability cluster with 2 or more routers. Advanced options are available in the Advanced pages.
h3: Cluster Configuration
config.enabled [CBI.FlagValue] Enable HA Cluster: [x]
  help: Enable high availability clustering on this router
config.node_priority [CBI.Value] Priority: value=150 (placeholder "100")
  help: VRRP priority (1-255). Higher priority becomes MASTER.
config.vrrp_transport [CBI.ListValue] VRRP Transport: select=unicast {multicast,unicast}
  help: Multicast is the default. Use unicast when multicast is unavailable on the network. Unicast adverts go to the peers below, from the first Source Address set: this fits only failover groups on the peers' network; another group sets its own unicast addresses in Advanced VRRP.
h3: Peer Routers
Other routers of the cluster. Configuration and lease sync run with every peer not marked VRRP only. In unicast mode, VRRP adverts are sent to every peer listed here, except for failover groups with their own unicast peers.
| Peer | Role | 
| peer1: ha-node2 (172.30.0.11) | Cluster node | [☰][Edit][Delete]
| peer2: edge-router (fd00:172:30::20) | VRRP only | [☰][Edit][Delete]
| peer3: legacy (172.30.0.12) | Cluster node | [☰][Edit][Delete]
<button> Add
h3: Virtual IP Addresses
All VIPs share a single failover group and switch together. Use the Advanced page to create independent failover groups. Multicast VRRP adds a second instance with VRID+128 for the IPv6 addresses. Unicast VRRP runs one instance in the family of the unicast addresses, and the other family fails over with it.
| Interface | VRID | IPv4 Address | IPv6 Address | Enable | 
| lan: <img> lan | 51 | 192.168.50.254 | fd00:192:168:50::254 | Yes | [☰][Edit][Delete]
| lan_old: <img> lan | 51 | 192.168.50.253 | none | No | [☰][Edit][Delete]
| vpn6: <img> backend | 52 | none | fd00:172:30::254 | Yes | [☰][Edit][Delete]
<button> Add VIP...
h3: Synchronization
Keeps configuration files and DHCP leases identical on the cluster nodes. These settings must be the same on every node.
config.encryption_key [CBI.Value] Encryption Key: password=0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef (placeholder "Click "Generate New Key" below to create a secure random key") button "∗"
  help: 256-bit AES key (64 hexadecimal characters), used for both configuration and lease sync. Must be identical on all nodes. Leave empty to sync in plaintext.
config._generate_key [CBI.ButtonValue] Generate New Key: button "Generate New Key"
h3: Configuration Files
config._owsync_missing [CBI.DummyValue] : text "owsync is not installed. Install the owsync package to synchronize configuration files. The 4 enabled sync groups in the configuration will apply once it is installed."
h3: DHCP Leases
config._lease_sync_missing [CBI.DummyValue] : text "lease-sync is not installed. Install the lease-sync and dnsmasq-ha packages to synchronize DHCP leases. Lease sync is on in the configuration and will start once they are installed."
==== simple modal peer1
h4: High Availability - General
peer1.name [CBI.Value] Peer Name: value=ha-node2 (placeholder "router2")
peer1.address [CBI.Value] Peer IP Address: value=172.30.0.11 (placeholder "192.168.1.2")
peer1.source_address [CBI.ListValue] Source Address: select=172.30.0.10 {,172.30.0.10,fd00:172:30::10,192.168.50.10,fd00:192:168:50::10}
  help: Local IP to use when contacting this peer. Must match address family (IPv4/IPv6) of peer.
peer1.vrrp_only [CBI.FlagValue] VRRP only: [ ]
  help: Tick for a router that does not run ha-cluster, for example a non-OpenWrt VRRP router. It is excluded from configuration and lease sync. In unicast mode keepalived still sends it VRRP adverts.
<button> Dismiss
<button> Save
